> Error in checkcovar(cross, pheno.col, addcovar, intcovar, perm.strata,  :
>   addcovar should be numeric
> In addition: Warning message:
> In checkcovar(cross, pheno.col, addcovar, intcovar, perm.strata,  :
>   Dropping 1 individuals with missing phenotypes.
> then
> > out.m <- scanone(male, addcovar=sex)
> Error in checkcovar(cross, pheno.col, addcovar, intcovar, perm.strata,  :
>   Number of rows in additive covariates is incorrect
> In addition: Warning message:
> In checkcovar(cross, pheno.col, addcovar, intcovar, perm.strata,  :
>   Dropping 1 individuals with missing phenotypes.

If you're doing the analysis with just the males, you don't want to
include sex as a covariate.

And when you do use sex as a covariate, you need to make sure that it's
numeric (0/1 values) not logical (TRUE/FALSE values). And that its
length is the same as the cross that you're using.

Here's some additional code to experiment with:

sex <- as.numeric(pull.pheno(mymap.bwg3, "sex")=="M")
male <- subset(mymap.bwg3, ind=(sex==1))

length(sex)
nind(male)
table(sex)
table( sex==1 )
sex[1:5]
(sex==1)[1:5]

karl

